runtime: make SSH child authority interruption-safe

Mask supported interruptions across pipe and PID acquisition and each
wait/status/PID-invalidation transition. Cleanup must retain an unreaped
child and must never signal its numeric PID after a successful reap or
ECHILD. Close acquired endpoints before leaving protected cleanup.

Keep the ordinary discovery loop interruptible and preserve native scan
results, deadlines and output limits. Only the SSH-specific child is owned;
this grants no guest or runner cleanup authority.
